      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653",
      "widgets_values": [
        "SAM3 MATTE TEST (stand-alone: nothing here touches the relight workflow)\n\n1. Type what to matte in the node 'WHAT TO MATTE' (e.g. person, woman, man in a red jacket). Keep it short: the limit is 32 tokens. Several targets: separate with commas.\n2. Run. 'Track preview' shows each tracked object over the plate; 'Matte preview' shows the combined matte.\n3. A ProRes matte is saved (..._sam3_matte) so you can compare it with the SAM2 matte in Nuke.\n\nFrame cap is 49 for a quick test (VoltLoader frame_load_cap; 0 = whole shot). Working size 1280 in the resize node.\n\nTO COMPARE WITH SAM2 look at: edges (hair, fingers), wobble over time, whether it picks the right person, and run time.\n'max_objects' on SAM3 track = how many things it will follow (default 4). 'detection_threshold' lower = finds more, higher = stricter.\n\nLICENCE: SAM3 uses Meta's SAM licence (royalty-free; indemnity, weight-redistribution and other terms). Have it read before client use. SAM2 is Apache-2.0."
      ]
    }
